# Dashboard and UI workflow guidance

Use this rule when editing the upload flow, session state, chart panels, or export UI.

## Architectural expectations

- `src/store/session-store.ts` is the bridge between uploaded files and rendered analysis.
- `src/App.tsx` decides whether the user sees the upload flow or the dashboard.
- Most dashboard components are consumers of the analysis payload; avoid duplicating analysis logic in UI components.

## UI change guidelines

- Keep chart components focused on presentation and light derivation.
- Prefer adding or refining computed data in `analysis-engine.ts` rather than scattering calculations across panels.
- Maintain loading, error, and empty-state behavior when touching the upload flow.
- If a component depends on optional analysis fields, guard for missing data rather than assuming everything is populated.

## PDF export

- `src/lib/pdf-export.ts` is part of the user-visible workflow.
- If dashboard content changes materially, think about whether export output should also change.
